      "message": "Sorry I had missed this when I asked you to make the class static.\nPassing the alert observer is fine because it\u0027s an immutable ref to an object that shares its lifetime with the enclosing class, but passing this array so that the individual callbacks can mutate it seems a bit unexpected.\n\nYou could :\n• have an interface to unregister a callback (unregisterCallback(Callback) or something), make NetworkStatsService (or some internal object) implement that, and pass it to instances of this class that would then call mUnregisterProxy.unregisterCallback(this)\n• do the same thing without an interface and simply pass the NetworkStatsService instance or the internal object\n• consider replacing the CopyOnWriteArrayList with an instance of android.os.RemoteCallbackList",
